  "definition": "Radiometric spacecraft navigation uses radio-link observables to estimate a spacecraft trajectory. The principal deep-space measurements are range, Doppler and very-long-baseline angular data. Each is a scalar or small set of observables tied to a signal path, station geometry, frequency reference and epoch. Orbit determination combines them with a dynamical model; it does not read a full position and velocity directly from the radio.[^1][^4]",
